
<p>A note flagged “Important” atop the Xcode 27.2 release notes:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>The iOS SDK and simulator support for iPhone Duo will be available
later this month in an upcoming release of Xcode 27.1.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>Adapting apps for the Duo is not just a simple “recompile with the new SDK”. It’s different. For just about all apps it’s going to be a significant amount of work, and for some apps it’s going to be a <em>lot</em> of work. But without Xcode 27.1, developers cannot get started. Developers wanted this SDK a week ago. And when day one preorder buyers start using their Duos on October 23, they’re going to wish Apple had shipped this SDK last week too.</p>

